From: Carlos Martins <cjom@reglinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: detect Linux by CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME as well as LINUX

The LINUX variable is computed once, while CMake determines the system,
from the CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME the toolchain file asked for. Buildroot's
toolchain file asks for a system named "Buildroot" so that its own
Platform/Buildroot.cmake gets picked up, and that module then does

    # Impersonate a Linux system. After all, that's what we are...
    set(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME Linux)
    include(Platform/Linux)

By then LINUX has already been decided and is false, so the platform
dispatch falls through to the else branch and aborts with the (rather
confusing) message

    CMake Error at CMakeLists.txt:172 (message):
      Unknown system Linux

naming the very system it just failed to recognise.

Accept either spelling, and set LINUX in that branch too: it is not only a
dispatch flag but is exported to dosbox_config.h as a #cmakedefine, where
it gates cdrom_ioctl_linux.cpp in its entirety, the Linux branch of
dos_mscdex.cpp, and part of sdl_gui.cpp. Leaving it false builds and links
fine but silently drops the host CD-ROM ioctl support.

Signed-off-by: Carlos Martins <cjom@reglinux.org>
---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 8d6208e..a44a621 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -165,7 +165,10 @@ elseif (APPLE)
   set(DOSBOX_PLATFORM_MACOS ON)
   set(MACOSX ON)
 
-elseif (LINUX)
+elseif (LINUX OR CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Linux")
+  # Also normalise LINUX itself: it is exported to dosbox_config.h via
+  # #cmakedefine and gates real code (cdrom_ioctl_linux.cpp, mscdex).
+  set(LINUX ON)
   set(DOSBOX_PLATFORM_LINUX ON)
 
 else()
